Z||000002||Sillhouette.com||01-21-2001||12:15 AM||||That one was done just for the picture.  It's a standard headlight system whos switch was forced to off halfway through it's travel.  You can tell that the parking lights are still on.   To do this properly you need to find a set of lights that you wish to install than play with it about a day adjusting the lifting arm to whatever hight you want.  <P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||01-21-2001||12:54 AM||||Actually, those headlights are from another car. They have been custom fit with brackets and a different bulb style. There is a stop installed on the arm so the headlight motors shut off when they hit that point. But, thats all the further they ever come up. I am still wanting to do that to my car useing HID lights, but need to save the money first.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BAM-BAM||01-21-2001||01:00 AM||||  Check this out! It's RSM's Slimline conversion. You'll have to get ahold of RSM for pricing. <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/slim.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/slim.jpg</A><P> Here's their main page link.   <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/main.html" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/main.html</A> <P>  Peace, B2 OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 01-21-2001).]||||reg||12
