Z||000013||lawrence||01-22-2001||12:26 PM||||The first car (the one with the air dam) is mine.  Technically, the lights aren't legal because I did't pay the big bucks to get DOT approval.  However, I used a standard headlight as the fixture, so it has the correct lens pattern.  Basically, I removed the inner single filament bulb and replaced it with a 9007 dual filament bulb.  I have a rough draft of a write up if you are interested in more detail:<P> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe/other/fiero/lowprofile.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe/other/fiero/lowprofile.htm</A> <P>I guess they do make the car look a little wacky, or maybe sleepy?  One thing nice, you can barely see the tops of them from the driver's seat.<P>Good luck,<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://www.webelectricmagazine.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.webelectricmagazine.com</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe/products" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe/products</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||the need for speed||01-23-2001||06:25 AM||||are there any lights small enough to do the rms style headlights that are not fog lights? What about the acura integra are those small enough to fit and have the right light pattern?I wounder what they are useing on this 300zx?<P><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jacquemond.com/300a6_small.jpg">   <P>[This message has been edited by the need for speed (edited 01-23-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by the need for speed (edited 01-23-2001).]||||reg||1
